Key assumptions requiring validation
The prototype should explicitly flag these points:

The exact policy formula for generating the monthly list and reserve list.
Whether the allocation is monthly, annual or represented through another reporting period.
The authoritative list of reasons a random selection cannot be completed.
When a reserve must or may be used.
Whether reserve order is predetermined.
How rolled-over records affect monthly statistics.
How attempted, completed and valid tests are defined.
How inconclusive and rejected samples affect reporting.
Whether a month can be closed with outstanding results.
What information must be entered into NOMIS.
What information must be included in a case note.
The required workflow for placing a prisoner on report.
The status of the digital record as legal evidence.
Retention, archival and deletion requirements.
Required roles and access controls.
Whether the MDT officer may amend incorrect information and how corrections must be recorded.
How prisoners who transfer between establishments are handled.
Whether lists may be regenerated and how a reset is authorised.
What establishment-level or national reports are required.
Which local variations are legitimate and which should be standardised.